# ==============================================================================
# SecureLock Web Console — Environment Variables Template
# ==============================================================================
# INSTRUCTIONS:
# 1. Copy this file to '.env' in the 'web' folder:
#    cp .env.example .env
# 2. Fill in your live Firebase credentials (optional - the console will run in
#    Cybersecurity Simulator / Demo mode if credentials are left blank).
# 3. DO NOT commit your actual '.env' file or any private keys to Git.
# ==============================================================================

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. Map Provider Configuration
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SecureLock uses OpenStreetMap tiles via Leaflet by default.
# OpenStreetMap is free, open-source, and DOES NOT REQUIRE AN API KEY or credit card.
# The interactive map renders out of the box with zero external configuration.
#
# If you optionally want to use custom Carto or Mapbox tiles:
# VITE_MAP_TILE_URL=https://tile.openstreetmap.org/{z}/{x}/{y}.png
# VITE_MAP_API_KEY=your_optional_tile_provider_key_here

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 2. Firebase Client Configuration (Web App)
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Obtain these from: Firebase Console -> Project Settings -> General -> Your apps -> Web app
# Note: Firebase Web API keys identify your project in Google Cloud, but should still
# have HTTP Referrer restrictions configured in the Google Cloud Console.
VITE_FIREBASE_API_KEY=your_firebase_api_key_here
VITE_FIREBASE_AUTH_DOMAIN=your_project_id.firebaseapp.com
VITE_FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=your_project_id
VITE_FIREBASE_STORAGE_BUCKET=your_project_id.appspot.com
VITE_FIREBASE_MESSAGING_SENDER_ID=your_messaging_sender_id
VITE_FIREBASE_APP_ID=your_firebase_app_id

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 3. CRITICAL SECURITY NOTICE
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# - NEVER store Firebase Admin SDK private keys ('serviceAccountKey.json') in this file
#   or in any client-side web directory. Service account keys grant full administrative
#   root access to Firestore/Auth and must strictly remain on a secure backend server.
# - In Google Cloud Console (APIs & Services -> Credentials), restrict your client API
#   keys to authorized HTTP referrers (e.g. 'https://securelock-mdc.vercel.app/*').
# ==============================================================================
